# React Functional Components

Always define React components as arrow functions. Do not use `function` declarations for components.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
function MyComponent({ title }: Props) {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
}

export function MyComponent({ title }: Props) {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
}

// ✅ GOOD
const MyComponent = ({ title }: Props) => {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
};

export const MyComponent = ({ title }: Props) => {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
};
```

- Use `const ComponentName = (...) => { ... }` for all components, including pages, layouts, and UI primitives.
- Named `function` declarations are fine for non-component helpers (hooks internals, utilities, event handlers) inside a file.
